sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ha08-24> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The trichia is caught entering but never leaving the Black Sea because it alone swims north into the Danube and, where the river divides, down into the Adriatic.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The trichia leaves the Black Sea up the Danube into the Adriatic";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, The History of Animals (Historia Animalium), Book VIII, Part 13; translated by D'Arcy Wentworth Thompson, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. IV (1910). Scope: trichia (probably a sardine or shad) in the Black Sea, Danube and Adriatic"
}
